From: omc-web <build@local>
Subject: [PATCH] gc: fix GC_deinit when threads are disabled on non-Windows

When building Boehm GC without threads on a non-Windows target (the wasm
case), the `!defined(GC_PTHREADS)` branch in GC_deinit tries to call
DeleteCriticalSection, which is a Win32 API. Constrain the call to the
Windows path so non-Windows no-thread builds compile.

--- a/misc.c
+++ b/misc.c
@@ -1463,7 +1463,7 @@
 #     if defined(THREADS) && (defined(MSWIN32) || defined(MSWINCE))
         DeleteCriticalSection(&GC_write_cs);
 #      endif
-#     if !defined(GC_PTHREADS)
+#     if !defined(GC_PTHREADS) && (defined(MSWIN32) || defined(MSWINCE))
         DeleteCriticalSection(&GC_allocate_ml);
 #     endif
     }
